:"நீர்","parts":[{"text":"நீர்","lemma":"நீர்","gloss":"water"}],"gloss":"water"},{"surface":"திகழ்","parts":[{"text":"திகழ்","lemma":"திகழ்","gloss":"shining"}],"gloss":"shining"},{"surface":"சிலம்பின்","parts":[{"text":"சிலம்பு","lemma":"சிலம்பு","gloss":"mountain slope"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of the mountain slope"},{"surface":"ஓராங்கு","parts":[{"text":"ஓராங்கு","lemma":"ஓராங்கு","gloss":"together"}],"gloss":"together"},{"surface":"அவிழ்ந்த","parts":[{"text":"அவிழ்ந்த","lemma":"அவிழ்","gloss":"blossomed"}],"gloss":"blossomed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வெண்","parts":[{"text":"வெண்","lemma":"வெண்மை","gloss":"white"}],"gloss":"white"},{"surface":"கூதாளத்து","parts":[{"text":"கூதாளத்து","lemma":"கூதாளத்து","gloss":"of the kūtāḷam plant"}],"gloss":"of the kūtāḷam plant","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அம்","parts":[{"text":"அம்","lemma":"அம்","gloss":"beautiful"}],"gloss":"beautiful"},{"surface":"தூம்பு","parts":[{"text":"தூம்பு","lemma":"தூம்பு","gloss":"tube"}],"gloss":"tube-like"},{"surface":"புது","parts":[{"text":"புது","lemma":"புதுமை","gloss":"new"}],"gloss":"new"},{"surface":"மலர்","parts":[{"text":"மலர்","lemma":"மலர்","gloss":"flower"}],"gloss":"flower"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆர்","parts":[{"text":"ஆர்","lemma":"ஆர்","gloss":"tightness"}],"gloss":"tight-fitting"},{"surface":"கழல்","parts":[{"text":"கழல்","lemma":"கழல்","gloss":"ring"}],"gloss":"ring"},{"surface":"புகுவ","parts":[{"text":"புகுவ","lemma":"புகு","gloss":"entering"}],"gloss":"entering"},{"surface":"போல","parts":[{"text":"போல","lemma":"போல","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சோர்குவ","parts":[{"text":"சோர்","lemma":"சோர்","gloss":"slip"},{"text":"குவ","lemma":"குவ","gloss":"neuter plural suffix"}],"gloss":"will slip"},{"surface":"அல்ல","parts":[{"text":"அல்ல","lemma":"அல்","gloss":"not"}],"gloss":"not"},{"surface":"என்பர்","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"என்","gloss":"say"},{"text":"பர்","lemma":"பர்","gloss":"they"}],"gloss":"will they say"},{"surface":"கொல்","parts":[{"text":"கொல்","lemma":"கொல்","gloss":"interrogative particle"}],"gloss":"indeed?"},{"surface":"நமர்","parts":[{"text":"நமர்","lemma":"நமர்","gloss":"our lover"}],"gloss":"our lover"},{"surface":"ஏ","parts":[{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"indeed"}]}],"literal":"Of the ripe millet on the red high ground thriving / of the clamorous sprouts in the dark night single leaf / the newborn fawn of the deer bites and performs its duty / seeing the rain-confronting cool field, the hand bangles / on the water-shining mountain slope all at once blossomed / of the white kūtāḷam plant's beautiful hollow new flowers / like entering the tight-fitting rings / will they not slip off? Will he say so, our man?","translation":"On the red high ground, the ripe millet thrives. In the dark night, a newborn deer fawn bites and feeds on the single-leaved, clamorous sprouts of millet, fulfilling its daily need. If I see this cool field welcoming the rains, will my hand bangles not slip off? Would our lover really say they won't, as if they were entering the tight hollows of the newly blossomed white kūtāḷam flowers on the water-glistening mountain slope?","modern":"செம்மையான மேட்டு நிலத்தில் செழித்து வளர்ந்த வரகின், கரிய இருளில் முளைத்த ஒற்றை இலையைக் கவ்வி உண்டு இளமான் தன் பசியைத் தீர்க்கும். கார் காலத்தை வரவேற்கும் இக்குளிர்ந்த புனத்தைக் காணும்போது, நீர் வழியும் மலைச்சரிவில் ஒரே சேர மலர்ந்த வெண்கூதாளத்தின் குழல் போன்ற புதிய மலர்களுக்குள் வண்டுகள் புகுவது போல, என் கைகளில் உள்ள வளையல்கள் கழன்று வீழாமல் இருக்குமா? நம் தலைவர் அவ்வாறு கழலாது என்று கூறுவாரோ?","explanation":"The heroine's friend speaks to the heroine about the arrival of the rainy season, which is the promised time of the hero's return. The poem is set in the Pālai landscape, transitioning into the seasonal return. The friend points out the signs of the season: the thriving millet on the red high ground, the young deer feeding on the fresh sprouts, and the blossoming of the white kūtāḷam flowers on the wet mountain slopes. The hollow, tube-like kūtāḷam flowers are compared to tight rings or bangles. The heroine's grief of separation has made her thin, causing her bangles to slip off. The friend questions whether the hero could possibly claim that her bangles would not slip off upon seeing these unmistakable signs of the season, urging him to return quickly.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}